+/// A schema file whose checksum matches but whose JSON breaks a rule of the schema (written
+/// by hand, or by an older version) fails the startup too: the strict deserialization runs
+/// after the checksum, and nothing in the file is renumbered or defaulted.
+#[test]
+fn audit_e1_verified_schema_file_with_repeated_or_missing_ids_fails_the_startup() {
